\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. On all the earth Thy spirit shower;
\par The earth in righteousness renew;
\par Thy kingdom come, and hell's o'erpower,
\par And to Thy sceptre all subdue.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Like mighty winds, or torrents fierce,
\par Let it opposers all o'errun;
\par And every law of sin reverse,
\par That faith and love may make all alone.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Yea, let Thy Spirit in every place
\par Its richer energy declare;
\par While lovely tempers, fruits of grace,
\par The kingdom of Thy Christ prepare.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Grant this, O holy God and true!
\par The ancient seers Thou didst inspire;
\par To us perform the promise due;
\par Descend, and crown us now with fire.
\par                                                Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

